[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-71809"] :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type I region has the property that a vertical line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type I region is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/d74059ee4370e106b54917ec43b007327805049033752867473d08da850001bf.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-71816"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/438b119b6fd2c2f066705f9f44053faa766e3f57b6ee1a614794febf7a517a12.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type I region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type I region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $x:$\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{y-3}\\,⟹\\,y={x}^{2}+3\n$$\n\nThe function $y=1$ is already written as a function of $x.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the vertical lines $x=0$ and $x=1.$ So, we have $0\\le x\\le 1.$\n\nWe draw a vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower function $g(x)$ and the upper function $f(x).$ A vertical line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type I region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/43b35101f6c57352975f3667ca76dece5782326c9af008990c8820a71bed504d.png)\n\nThe vertical line enters the region through the lower function $y=1$ and leaves through the upper function $y={x}^{2}+3.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+3.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-72045/selection/c755e4d6e156de15d236b0a150d5d117219b46316207c09cf4e8b4ec71d6219c" :answer/id #uuid "642c7741-77fa-58c4-81f7-b3f5d733543b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/8ce69ec8237ba99ebc6cd75ba1dc26e592e7af1d45fb2b2d06c918ecbeae8785.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72045/selection/b919ae716e254b95a52e3d10793cf24a75e42a2bda7f7e15275cbb62309199e7" :answer/id #uuid "16dcf353-8254-5bd7-9284-e7b7d14aeed2" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/63a6ace387d56a8b789316123a12fe621b0605d10f887c84c5c9d7c17f68b1bf.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72045/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" :answer/id #uuid "93c075e4-af5b-5b9c-910a-723958c2ca08" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72045/selection/8b5951cd2fb5f5110e203f9f32434720934337574786a17c4b577c7c01f92e46" :answer/id #uuid "ffa5ea8f-0abf-5e18-8f59-101c20e92086" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/f327774382e0dca490b4b05bb971c97ae44fdcd4c9434a898591b816ae491e28.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72045/selection/e11b909d50d9e77614824983f0cccd4b1ebf31abbbc68c3f7d92f73bc39a4614" :answer/id #uuid "d97524fd-87c0-54f5-b570-cdceaa35c4aa" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/r