pe :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72038/selection/606348fabc4a46e7202e82c2e4dc33fbbf511f160d30ac52069d54a5e08c73b9" :answer-field/choices ["q-72038/selection/59b809dc47a33256f409e978e09b2a2bafe20d3c6e41e137383fd57bf80928bc" "q-72038/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" "q-72038/selection/606348fabc4a46e7202e82c2e4dc33fbbf511f160d30ac52069d54a5e08c73b9" "q-72038/selection/bfaa4723958924a195286b97af476efd3f2d48d5ea91963b02b16c44bded04b7" "q-72038/selection/094c5eb67fa6706f33cdc50f7658de61f19036a80f5f37827932d3aa5859cad7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72038" :question/id #uuid "a8a8de6a-3043-5d0c-ae35-56392ae16ec8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72038" :question/problem "Which of the following is a type I region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type I region has the property that a vertical line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type I region is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/af08994008c1df01d052fbc345e6892fed33b7d82ad2de5eb55089e9a879e602.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72038/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d342be-ebaf-5e94-b641-ea8ce6f14c12"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72038"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73532/selection/07966797818510fa74a56751cd36c5ef3c3478f6d5b986f7b512d9397a038d48" :answer/id #uuid "c19dd8db-321b-5a04-8a6d-2464c52803a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73532/selection/7b50bf3a72c08e7158698b5db5a6d58df2717da0ffd28e144a46d038e99ede11" :answer/id #uuid "62a50ee6-80f9-5e55-8bbd-05a650d8c085" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}+1\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73532/selection/afbdf800136a306a9fae076ce558353336272a865e9620f710ab5a1a292119f5" :answer/id #uuid "7b920f50-2ccc-5392-922a-1341e3c1bdf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}+3\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73532/selection/e75ac88bb98327977a264e91b713f15b86161e4ca27de6cff5cbf687d1674003" :answer/id #uuid "8c1bdea2-0bb8-5bb6-ae9e-62a3e14c8638" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73532/selection/01a31f3087a9714665649f86eb6c6a46dc6ef9d815964ed4f0554b317499cf4a" :answer/id #uuid "9b882010-5288-5d0a-bbff-29b6ad594ed7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-{x}^{2}+3\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73532/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "22c2f92c-84cf-5c4e-8386-899599683563" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73532/selection/7b50bf3a72c08e7158698b5db5a6d58df2717da0ffd28e144a46d038e99ede11" :answer-field/choices ["q-73532/selection/07966797818510fa74a56751cd36c5ef3c3478f6d5b986f7b512d9397a038d48" "q-73532/selection/7b50bf3a72c08e7158698b5db5a6d58df2717da0ffd28e144a46d038e99ede11" "q-73532/selection/afbdf800136a306a9fae076ce558353336272a865e9620f710ab5a1a292119f5" "q-73532/selection/e75ac88bb98327977a264e91b713f15b86161e4ca27de6cff5cbf687d1674003" "q-73532/selection/01a31f3087a9714665649f86eb6c6a46dc6ef9d815964ed4f0554b317499cf4a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73532" :question/id #uuid "5386da7a-d4e3-5516-bd15-c0227ea4ae2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-73532" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/d69e6b6550f7e4cae0785daaa19c0a52382a595c40309dccd1d832dbc6d2f82f.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type I region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type I region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $x:$\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{y-1}+1\\,⟹\\,y=(x-1)^{2}+1\n$$\n\nThe function $y=-(x-1)^{2}+3$ is already written as a function of $x.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the vertical lines $x=1$ and $x=2.$ So, we have $1\\le x\\le 2.$\n\nWe draw a vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower function $g(x)$ and the upper function $f(x).$ A vertical line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type I region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/942a39f885e6f88bef997e27914d05359be86ae1d6204f3834f0829ce4b81136.png)\n\nThe vertical line enters the region through the lower function $y=(x-1)^{2}+1$ and leaves through the upper function $y=-(x-1)^{2}+3.$ So, we have $(x-1)^{2}+1\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+3.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}+1\\le y\\le -(x-1)^{2}+3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73532/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64d342be-ebaf-5e94-b641-ea8ce6f14c12"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73532"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-168140/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" :answer/id #uuid "0f78d1c2-aae9-567e-bd4b-a04931822ec1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None 