\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/fe16f5f3d1e9663a7e0df88d71639016bfb3357a6745ee6f125968978fd54c12.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72055/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85335de6-e1dc-5a2f-b30a-806627759030"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72055"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73552/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "3f0aee89-7f16-5494-b654-c3abcf640fa6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73552/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "42e01d55-865b-507a-8469-a108bc7d61f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73552/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "7c5bc784-ec8d-5fe7-861e-c5847e2ec08a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73552/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "72f7ea34-2bbb-5fc4-8d46-c698ee992a61" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73552/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "1aa59bbc-9d00-5444-9de6-5cdb50f05706" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73552/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "79f23227-eb8d-5c3e-9c36-7a1ee7738ab1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73552/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-73552/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-73552/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-73552/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-73552/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-73552/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73552" :question/id #uuid "964e90c7-3ddc-59ef-9c19-6cc6da31e561" :question/math-academy-id "q-73552" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the ellipses $(x-1)^{2}+4{y}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=4?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/215dd0c920e700a75896fc54751ec20d197487a2c992cd8910810c66129c14dc.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/7e1a0c5dd2b4aadf7efe78d903234b8d00cf4fa92eb7a3b41209a856f2d14b01.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=0.25$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/a90d7306e3f88a31609e368f9362248d6a12b7922b6a9e8c9f980ab31e7fb140.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73552/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73552"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72185/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "1a0f3222-a5f8-5fcd-b098-fcccf3105990" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72185/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "12f729bd-320f-50de-bd74-5b2cd483e355" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72185/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "81814992-97d4-5d06-b32c-f9c0ba5e739c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72185/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "fc67656a-c62a-5f24-8999-265587a5d457" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72185/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "4efd1cc1-35fd-5180-98b1-c020add13878" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72185/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2ceb530-70bd-5b73-b3ec-0ae8db0a36f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72185/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-72185/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-72185/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-72185/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-72185/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-72185/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72185" :question/id #uuid "a5dd306f-63b8-5be6-adf1-ac9dc3f00602" :question/math-academy-id "q-72185" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region inside the circumference ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,x=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1\\, & ⟹\\,y=\\pm \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/0960063edcce8ccd55dc2f77147c4a4982645c180e8b998d7e520c65131ea045.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-72185/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72185"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-168921/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "25a51b0b-8af3-5923-9476-50f086e4c490" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168921/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "ab679ae5-eed5-5735-a4d2-499a07ece9df" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168921/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "6436387b-b9e9-50bd-b385-025a30598c91" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168921/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "3e7a3a0b-4973-5888-83c9-755356b5af9e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168921/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "3a455fa3-2642-5412-95c0-be54ed74d7eb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-168921/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b14272d0-d3cf-572b-935f-630196f28670" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-168921/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-168921/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-168921/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-168921/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-168921/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-168921/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-168921" :question/id #uuid "fd6f7437-bc45-50cb-9400-bcd422c5b408" :question/math-academy-id "q-168921" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ and the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=1?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/bc6b71d1fe69abd34dbd939dc62ede5201b75713e25456cf084e889bc44f449e.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.4$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/4a1fd7069abaa3b3fa4d9c286773d226798bf3ad565e85663cab44557fd635c1.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=-1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/260e8e959ca95a029a98bd4102106a66df418ea73c0640398c8fdebfdbf812f6.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-168921/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-168921"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-71895"] :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circles ${x}^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/24cbd9a0e01023dca6a289838d94efe3c7b67abe5b7a1f275f6945f280e65d64.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.75$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/6c51abe5c21571a9c5596fce4e3b8ace210eacfab125016e6b9a3b2a7bc2e056.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/f9fed5856eda128d84debec320bc38a35eaa2bf5184b1f81cb1194b02f8a306a.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-72186/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "4f18db94-ad67-593f-b114-ebc6d5002eab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72186/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "eb524796-12ff-54a4-b598-cd196967e8ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72186/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "2a60cbe0-3aad-56b3-895f-48b7e3acfbaf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72186/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "a1e4f88d-10b3-5c3f-afff-d9d099368d46" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72186/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "674a9f4c-4b66-51bd-aab2-ed3d3dcd0e22" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72186/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2da88fc7-748c-5911-9d27-4eaa5cc1f0be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72186/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-72186/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-72186/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-72186/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-72186/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-72186/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72186" :question/id #uuid "ab932e6b-af0e-5e9b-9cca-659edaed65a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-72186" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the parabola $y=4-{x}^{2}$ and the line $y=2-|x|?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/6f35161e7efbd53c9ef558ffe88d8e046771128965a9fdd02143ae37a9b130ea.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,2-|x|\\le y\\le 4-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- The horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/769a521cd6b05ecf05052da382e40295b26be66fe56e4eff7c6940c9032f2f0b.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-72186/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7948909f-8dcb-5cc0-a00f-f505a41e4004"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72186"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6101"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/766a7abf73e9f9ef85164b1165166d7493cd36cdc75d0f244e475fed8aeea8fd.png)\n\nRepresent the type I region above using set notation." :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: a \\leq x  \\leq b, \\quad g(x) \\leq y \\leq f(x) \\big\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type I region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $x.$\n\n- The curve $x=y-1$ can be written as $y=x+1.$\n\n- The curve $y=7-x$ is already written as a function of $x.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the vertical lines $x=1$ and $x=3.$ So, we have $1 \\leq x \\leq 3.$\n\nWe draw a vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower function $g(x)$ and the upper function $f(x)$. A vertical line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type I region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/acf870e74a9029543a6e6b21995c293f67f251b54dfad9584220780bc3a0b454.png)\n\nThe vertical line enters the region through the lower function $y=x+1$ and leaves through the upper function $y=7-x.$ So, we have $x+1 \\leq y \\leq 7-x.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD= \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\: x+1 \\leq y \\leq 7-x \\big\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6102"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/3919a6a8442e983a9ca3465b2ed9abbeda18b7dc8d21b7c74b1851b53c1be714.png)\n\nRepresent the type II region above using set notation." :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: a \\leq y  \\leq b, \\quad g(y) \\leq x \\leq f(y) \\big\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y.$\n\n- The curve $y = 2-x^2$ can be written as $x = -\\sqrt{2-y}.$ Note that we have picked the negative square root since $x\\leq 0$ in our region.\n\n- The curve $x=\\dfrac{y-2}{2}$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=-2$ and $y=2.$ So, we have $-2 \\leq y \\leq 2.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y)$. A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/0cf258d0269db0977d5c19fe7abd159f13319bb493394fbd049e5660d88a1d6f.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=-\\sqrt{2-y}$ and leaves through the upper function $x=\\dfrac{y-2}{2}.$ So, we have $-\\sqrt{2-y} \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{y-2}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD= \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -2 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\: -\\sqrt{2-y} \\leq x \\leq \\dfrac{y-2}{2} \\bigg\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6103"] :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the parabola $y=x^2$ and the line $y=4?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n\n- It is a type II region\n\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\ny=x^2\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx = \\pm\\sqrt{y}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/59d32c44bae848d52adc188e15a8bab470b3eccd887cad45c231b66c486284fc.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -2 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: x^2 \\leq y \\leq 4 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 4, \\: -\\sqrt{y} \\leq x \\leq \\sqrt{y} \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
